RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
February 9, 2009
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met on this date beginning at 6:00 p.m. in
Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL MEMBERS - Ms.
Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Collins, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Spiker and
Mr. Valdez.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Dan White,
City Attorney.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and
support by two other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be
considered in its normal sequence on the agenda.) Upon request by Mayor Kaysen, and pursuant
to support received by Mr. Collins and Mr. Brown, agenda item #23(a) was removed from the
Consent Agenda.  Upon request by Mr. Collins, and pursuant to support received by Mr. Brown
and Ms. Ash, agenda item #20(c) was removed from the Consent Agenda.  Mayor Kaysen
clarified his request to remove item #23(a), Appointment, was due to provisions of state statute
that place restrictions on the mayor voting on a mayoral appointee. It was noted that
procedurally members did not need to officially provide a “second” to a request to remove
consent agenda items.  Mr. Brown moved to approve remaining Consent Agenda items,
seconded by Mr. Collins.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
JANUARY 26, 2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
FEBRUARY 2, 2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Valdez moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr.
Collins.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body.
“AN ORDINANCE AMENDING TITLE 17, ZONING, CHAPTER 17.08, ZONING
DISTRICTS ESTABLISHED AND SECTION 17.08.040 CHEYENNE CITY MAP OF THE
CHEYENNE CITY CODE 2002, BY CHANGING THE ZONING CLASSIFICATION FROM
CB COMMUNITY BUSINESS DISTRICT TO  HR-2 HIGH-DENSITY RESIDENTIAL-
DEVELOPING DISTRICT FOR LOT 6, BLOCK ONE, GATEWAY SOUTH, CHEYENNE,
WYOMING (LOCATED EAST OF WALTERSCHEID BOULEVARD AND SOUTH OF
WEST FOX FARM ROAD).” R.C. Reiman, manager for Gateway South, submitted a letter (on
file with City Clerk’s office) requesting postponement of the item to Feb. 23, 2009 to allow time
to continue negotiations regarding zone change issues.  Reporting for Public Services
Committee, Mr. Brown moved to approve on third and final reading, seconded by Mr. Pierson.
Mr. Brown moved to postpone for two weeks (to Feb. 23, 2009), seconded by Mr. Pierson.
