“A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING THE MAYOR AND THE CITY CLERK TO SIGN
A COUNTY FINAL PLAT FOR JEFFERSON HILLS SUBDIVISION, A REPLAT OF A
PORTION OF LOT 1, BLOCK 1, LEY SUBDIVISION AND TRACT 2, HERMANN
MEADOWS SUBDIVISION, LARAMIE COUNTY, WYOMING (LOCATED NORTH OF
AND ADJACENT TO E. JEFFERSON ROAD, EAST OF S. GREELEY HIGHWAY).” Mr.
Spiker declared a conflict of interest and indicated he would not be participating in discussion
and voting, and vacated Council Chambers.  Mr. Brown moved to adopt, seconded by Mr.
Pierson.  Mr. Brown moved to postpone to March 9, 2009, seconded by Dr. Rinne.  It was noted
a postponement was requested by the developer.  Motion to postpone carried.  Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body present in Council Chambers. Following announcement of the
vote, Mr. Spiker returned to Council Chambers.
“A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING THE MAYOR AND THE CITY CLERK TO SIGN
A COUNTY FINAL PLAT FOR SNOWARDT SUBDIVISION, A REPLAT OF THE SOUTH
120 FEET OF TRACT 4, CAPITOL TRACTS, LARAMIE COUNTY, WYOMING (LOCATED
NORTH OF AND ADJACENT TO HELLWIG ROAD, WEST OF YORK AVENUE).” Mr.
Brown moved to adopt with County conditions #1 through 5, seconded by Mr. Pierson.  Upon
inquiry, Abby Yenco, Laramie County Planning, provided information on County condition #5
involving a road status form and stated as there will be no changes to the road, the form would
not be required. Concern was expressed that the roadway width proposed (50 ft.) was not the
standard 60 ft. width contained in the current Road, Street and Site, Planning and Design
Standards.  Ms. Yenco  advised the final plat had been reviewed and adopted before but the time
frame for filing the plat had expired, and that the previous plat reflected a roadway width of 50
ft.  Discussion followed on including an additional 5 ft. of right-of-way on each side of the street
to ensure the roadway would meet future width compliance.  Mr. Pierson moved to amend by
modifying the 50 ft. roadway width to 60 ft. with 5 ft. of right-of-way added to each side of the
roadway, seconded by Mr. Collins.  Upon inquiry, Ms. Yenco stated if the amendment is
approved it will not affect adjacent properties until those properties are developed at which time
the additional right-of-way for roadway width would be required.  Motion to amend to increase
the roadway width to 60 ft. (additional 5 ft. of right-of-way on each side of the roadway) carried.
Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body.  Upon inquiry, Ms. Yenco advised the
County Commissioners have not yet acted upon the final plat.  Main motion as amended carried.
Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body.  (#5102)
